  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Ongoing political friction between Rahul Gandhi and the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) has intensified through a series of public critiques and rebuttals. Recently, Gandhi utilized an image of the Hindu deity Ardhanareshwar to label the BJP and the Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh (RSS) as casteist and chauvinistic. This followed previous exchanges where the BJP criticized Gandhi’s comments on the Prime Minister and national economic growth. Further conflict arose regarding the Manipur government, with Gandhi attributing recent fatalities from illicit alcohol consumption to administrative negligence. Simultaneously, government representatives like Kiren Rijiju have challenged Gandhi’s remarks by referencing past political history and national security issues. These events form part of a broader, sustained period of policy and ideological debate between the Congress party leadership and the incumbent government, as both sides continue to exchange accusations concerning regional governance and India's international positioning.",
